symbols.doc:
Original qualifier covers each exact (instruction, semantic_key) form.

Its premises cover the form's full admitted address/count/selector domain;
instruction spelling, exact-copy metadata and matching IDs are not proof.

Execute actual byte addresses, independently of the planner's mapping.

This synchronous host executor is useful for testing instruction adapters;
it supplies no device execution or timing qualification.

The ISA an ELF (an image or one object) records it was compiled for (``Tag_RISCV_arch``), as
``[base+first letter, extension, ...]`` without versions (``["rv64i", "m", ..., "v", "zvl128b"]``);
empty when it records none.
